WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.760
Tesla's model y is threatening to become South Korea's top-selling vehicle overall. This is Tesla Shorts Time,

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:14.680
episode 626. In South Korea, fsd remains quite limited, while buyers in the United States can purchase

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:22.040
and use the feature without restriction. TSLA Minging noted the contrast on X. The model y is closing

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:29.000
in on the Kia Serrento as the country's overall top-seller. Hyundai is turning to new SUVs and a small

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.420
electric car to recover from its weakest sales since the pandemic. Production disruptions

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.840
and tougher competition have hit the company at home and abroad. In China, the Model 3 now

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:46.640
ships with a 16-inch center display. The screen replaces the prior 15.4-inch unit and offers

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.760
sharper images plus a smoother refresh rate. Every Model 3 and Model Y variant there can

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:59.020
deliver up to 2.2 kilowatts of AC output through vehicle to load. That power level runs

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:04.740
a kettle, a rice cooker, and another appliance simultaneously. Tesla has not said the upgrades

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.800
will reach North America or Europe. The China only changes appear in the cool down.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:17.120
In Austin, the Robotaxi service now ends at 11 pm instead of 10. Elon Musk said the remaining

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:22.320
obstacle is avoiding pets that blend into dark pavement. He wrote that the main task

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.460
Ask is making sure the vehicles do not run over pets when they are hard to see at night.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.780
Motor One reported the update.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.600
Globally, the Model Y still led battery electric vehicle sales in August.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:43.120
BYD sold 375,373 vehicles that month, while Tesla sold 141,996.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:49.740
From January through August, BYD held a 20.3% share of global plug-in vehicle sales.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:55.180
Geely followed at 9.9% and Tesla at 8.3%.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.120
Digital today covered the rankings.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.800
Tesla delivered 486,532 vehicles in the third quarter.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.440
The figure beat expectations even though it felt 2% from the prior year.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.980
Baird kept its out-perform rating and $475 target.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:18.380
Analyst Gary Black calculated that sustained delivery gains could add $0.15 to annual adjusted

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:24.780
earnings per share, and $32 per share to the company's value. Yahoo Finance carried the note.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:31.120
Crew Dragon Grace reached the space station in seven hours and 55 minutes. NASA confirmed

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.940
the flight set the fastest launch to docking record for any U.S. spacecraft at the International

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:42.860
Space Station. The prior U.S. record also belonged to a Dragon capsule. Tesla Roddy reported the

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:48.620
milestone. A new software feature called emergency drive away lets drivers pull away from

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:54.440
a supercharger while still plugged in. The override works only on US superchargers and only

00:02:54.440 --> 00:03:00.920
after the latest update. Tesla warns that misuse can cause up to $25,000 in repair costs.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:07.520
Car and driver describe the safety update. In Canada, a rear-wheel drive Model 3 premium

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:16.340
list at $41,990 including freight. At current exchange rates, that equals just under $29,500

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:22.700
for a car with ventilated seats and a panoramic roof. The Canadian government rates the China-built

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:31.520
version at 15.3 kilowatt hours per 100 kilometers and 463 kilometers of range. The auto-topian noted

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:37.920
the tariff-driven import. A million mile trucker toured the Tesla semi-factory and shared first-hand

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:45.240
observations. Basinore posted the account. Japan's imported EV sales past 20,000 units in the

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:50.960
fiscal first half for the first time. Tesla accounted for roughly 70% of those sales.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:57.300
Finance Bigo reported the milestone. Tesla led imported car sales in Korea for the 8th

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:02.920
month in September. The Model Y finished as the single best-selling vehicle in the country during

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:08.960
that period. Korea Jung-ang daily carried the sales data. President Trump's September 29

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:14.640
executive order directed federal agencies to replace the term artificial intelligence with super

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:21.080
intelligence in official documents. Elon Musk said on October 4 that he would rename Space X AI

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:28.540
to space XSI. TSLA-minging traced the policy change back to the 1955 Dartmouth proposal

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:34.400
that launched the field. The post appears on X. A Motley Fool column examined whether

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:40.160
Tesla's recent delivery beat makes the stock attractive at current levels. TSLA-minging

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.300
asked what evidence would justify calling a system super-intelligent. The reply called

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.720
for sustained superiority across unfamiliar problems and multiple fields with human contributions

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:57.680
clearly separated. CXO today explored how China's underwater solar projects and orbital data center

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:04.140
ideas might intersect with Tesla's energy work. Drive Tesla Canada showed how higher utilization at

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:10.260
business site superchargers can cut energy costs for operators. Tesla is challenging its exclusion

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:15.960
from a Manitoba electric vehicle incentive program in court. The company argues the exclusion is

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.800
politically motivated and blocks fair market access. CBC reported the hearing.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:26.060
Battery chemistry choices forced direct trade-offs among cost, energy density,

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:31.040
and supply chain exposure. The smaller pack Model 3 imported into Canada

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.980
accepts reduced range to satisfied tariff rules and local pricing.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:41.460
The Canadian version carries roughly 70.8 kilowatt hours and 288 miles of range,

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:46.920
while the US model uses 78.1 kilowatt hours and 363 miles.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:52.840
That difference shifts its position against the Chevrolet Bolt, which offers 262 miles

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.200
at a slightly higher price.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:58.460
Supercharger safety rules also embed liability calculations.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:04.740
The emergency drive-away feature permits drivers to leave while connected, yet Tesla caps potential

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:10.640
repair costs at $25,000 and limits the feature to the United States after the current software

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:18.380
update. Pre-2021 Model S and Model X vehicles receive no support. Semi-manufacturing follows its

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:24.020
own durability logic. A million-mile trucker visiting the factory underscores the need for real

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:30.580
world mileage data that passenger programs rarely generate at scale. Early orders such as the 50 units

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:36.880
placed by IMC logistics will begin to test the original cost per mile assumptions. Before we go,

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:42.100
So watch for further clarity on how tariff-driven imports shape Model 3 pricing in additional

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:42.540
markets.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:45.840
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:54.960
TSLA closed at $378.73, up $8.14, or 2.2%.

